 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "foreignsurvey.governor (an independent Survey-Integrity Compliance
 Governor) in front of a contained foreignsurvey.foreignsurveyllm
 advisor, wired as a langgraph StateGraph (foreignsurvey.operation) with
 an interrupt-before approval node. Two flagship HARD checks, both from
 涉外调查管理办法 (国家统计局令第7号): foreign-survey-permit-missing /
 -elapsed / -validity-unknown (第十条 -- the conducting organization must
 hold a 涉外调查许可证 recorded AND unexpired at the field start date,
 checked at BOTH actuation ops), and social-survey-project-unapproved
 (第八条/第九条 -- ONLY 涉外社会调查 needs per-project approval;
 涉外市场调查 needs the permit alone, and holding a market survey on a
 missing approval would block legitimate research, so
 :per-project-approval-kinds is a CLOSED set rather than a boolean).
 Further HARD checks: prohibited-content against the closed
 seven-item 第七条 set (enforced at filing as well as fieldwork),
 survey-kind-unrecognized (第三条 -- an unclassified kind is NOT read as
 the more permissive 市场调查), sensitive-pi-without-separate-consent and
 cross-border-transfer-without-lawful-basis (PIPL, with the four
 第三十八条 bases as a closed set), and the fleet's MAXIMUM-ceiling family
 check on planned vs approved sample size with its own explicit
 un-checkable hold. :project/file and :survey/field are absent from every
 phase's :auto set, asserted at load time in foreignsurvey.phase."}
